# The witness co-signature verifier that lets a record earn EXTERNAL witness
# scope, and the test tools that check it. Compile with:
#   uv pip compile --no-header --python-version 3.12 requirements-witness.in -o requirements-witness.txt
# It is a separate environment, not a probity-verify extra: the pinned observer
# depends on the jcs-admit Python binding at a commit that still published it as
# probityai, the name of the probity command in this workspace, so the two
# cannot share one lock or one environment. jcs-admit now publishes the binding
# as jcs-admit; once the observer moves to it, this becomes a witness extra.
# probity-verify itself is installed with --no-deps, so its own dependencies
# are listed here.
